# THE FUNDAMENTAL THEOREM OF CALCULUS, for Riemann sums: the sums of a derivative converge to the difference of the
# function. F (written bigf) is UNIFORMLY DIFFERENTIABLE with derivative f when, for every tolerance eps > 0, a mesh
# w makes every step obey
#   |F(x + w) - F(x) - f(x) w| <= eps w,
# Bishop's definition of the derivative. For a partition of [a, b] into n strips of width w, points pt(0) = a,
# pt(i + 1) = pt(i) + w, the left Riemann sum is sum(0) = 0, sum(i + 1) = sum(i) + f(pt(i)) w, and the theorem is
#   |sum(n) - (F(pt(n)) - F(pt(0)))| <= eps n w = eps (b - a),
# for every n: the Riemann sums of f come within eps (b - a) of F(b) - F(a) once the mesh is fine enough for eps, so
# the integral of f over [a, b] IS F(b) - F(a). The proof is a telescoping induction over n (`fold n`), each step an
# instance of the derivative hypothesis, decided over an ordered field. F, f, pt and sum are quantified functions:
# the theorem holds for every function with a uniform derivative.
#
# THE HYPERBOLIC DISK. In space/hyperbolic/area the circle of radius r has circumference 2 pi sinh r and the area
# enclosed grows at that rate, so with F = cosh - 1 and f = sinh this theorem makes the disk's area the limit of its
# Riemann sums, 2 pi (cosh r - 1). The sums are also computed EXACTLY below: with C(i) = cosh(i h) and the midpoint
# sinh values M(i) = sinh((i + 1/2) h), the addition formula gives C(i + 1) - C(i) = 2 sinh(h/2) M(i) (from
# space/hyperbolic/archimedes: cosh(a + b) - cosh(a - b) = 2 sinh a sinh b), so the midpoint sum telescopes:
#   2 sinh(h/2) M(0) + ... + 2 sinh(h/2) M(n - 1) = cosh(n h) - 1,
# the area sum times h / (2 sinh(h/2)), a factor that tends to 1 with h.


# THE THEOREM, by induction on the number of strips n.
rule the-riemann-sums-of-a-derivative-approach-its-difference
  mark bigf
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark f
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark pt
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark sum
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark n, like integer
  mark w, like integer
  mark eps, like integer
  have the-points-are-evenly-spaced
    mark i, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read i
        code 0
      call is-equal
        call subtract
          call pt
            call add
              read i
              code 1
          call pt
            read i
        read w
  have bigf-has-derivative-f-at-the-mesh
    mark i, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read i
        code 0
      meet and
        call is-maximum
          call subtract
            call subtract
              call bigf
                call pt
                  call add
                    read i
                    code 1
              call bigf
                call pt
                  read i
            call multiply
              call f
                call pt
                  read i
              read w
          call multiply
            read eps
            read w
        call is-maximum
          call subtract
            call multiply
              call f
                call pt
                  read i
              read w
            call subtract
              call bigf
                call pt
                  call add
                    read i
                    code 1
              call bigf
                call pt
                  read i
          call multiply
            read eps
            read w
  have the-riemann-sum-starts-at-zero
    call is-equal
      call sum
        code 0
      code 0
  have the-riemann-sum-adds-a-strip
    mark i, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read i
        code 0
      call is-equal
        call sum
          call add
            read i
            code 1
        call add
          call sum
            read i
          call multiply
            call f
              call pt
                read i
            read w
  have the-width-is-positive
    call is-above
      read w
      code 0
  have the-tolerance-is-not-negative
    call is-minimum
      read eps
      code 0
  have n-is-a-count
    call is-minimum
      read n
      code 0
  show hold
    meet and
      call is-maximum
        call subtract
          call sum
            read n
          call subtract
            call bigf
              call pt
                read n
            call bigf
              call pt
                code 0
        call multiply
          call multiply
            read eps
            read n
          read w
      call is-maximum
        call subtract
          call subtract
            call bigf
              call pt
                read n
            call bigf
              call pt
                code 0
          call sum
            read n
        call multiply
          call multiply
            read eps
            read n
          read w
  fold n


# THE STRIP OF THE DISK. For pairs on the hyperbola (cosh, sinh), cosh(a + b) - cosh(a - b) = 2 sinh a sinh b: with
# a = (i + 1/2) h and b = h / 2 this is C(i + 1) - C(i) = 2 sinh(h/2) M(i).
rule the-addition-formula-gives-the-strip
  mark ca, like integer
  mark sa, like integer
  mark cb, like integer
  mark sb, like integer
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call subtract
        call add
          call multiply
            read ca
            read cb
          call multiply
            read sa
            read sb
        call subtract
          call multiply
            read ca
            read cb
          call multiply
            read sa
            read sb
      call multiply
        call multiply
          code 2
          read sa
        read sb


# THE DISK AREA SUM, exactly: if each strip obeys C(i + 1) - C(i) = 2 s M(i) (s = sinh(h/2)), the sum of the strips
# 2 s M(i) is C(n) - C(0) = cosh(n h) - 1, for every n: the midpoint area sum, times the factor 2 s / h.
rule the-disk-area-sum-telescopes
  mark cc
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark mid
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark acc
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark n, like integer
  mark s, like integer
  have each-strip-is-a-difference
    mark i, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read i
        code 0
      call is-equal
        call subtract
          call cc
            call add
              read i
              code 1
          call cc
            read i
        call multiply
          call multiply
            code 2
            read s
          call mid
            read i
  have the-sum-starts-at-zero
    call is-equal
      call acc
        code 0
      code 0
  have the-sum-adds-a-strip
    mark i, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read i
        code 0
      call is-equal
        call acc
          call add
            read i
            code 1
        call add
          call acc
            read i
          call multiply
            call multiply
              code 2
              read s
            call mid
              read i
  have n-is-a-count
    call is-minimum
      read n
      code 0
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call acc
        read n
      call subtract
        call cc
          read n
        call cc
          code 0
  fold n


# COSH IS UNIFORMLY DIFFERENTIABLE WITH DERIVATIVE SINH, from two elementary facts about the pair: the addition
# formula cosh(a + b) = cosh a cosh b + sinh a sinh b (archimedes.tree proves it is the boost composition), and the
# bounds near 0, 1 <= cosh w <= 1 + w^2 and w <= sinh w <= w + w^3 for 0 <= w <= 1 (true of the power series). Where
# cosh and sinh are at most big, a step of w changes cosh by sinh x w up to
#   0 <= cosh(x + w) - cosh(x) - sinh(x) w <= big (w^2 + w^3),
# which is the derivative hypothesis of the theorem above with eps = big (w + w^2), and eps -> 0 with the mesh. So the
# Riemann sums of sinh over [0, r] tend to cosh r - 1, and 2 pi times that is the area of the hyperbolic disk of
# radius r (its circumference is 2 pi sinh r, space/hyperbolic/metric). The certificate is the product prover's:
#   big w^2 + big w^3 - [..] = (big - cosh x)(cosh w - 1) + big (w^2 - cosh w + 1)
#                              + (big - sinh x)(sinh w - w) + big (w^3 - sinh w + w).
rule cosh-has-derivative-sinh
  mark cc
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark ss
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark x, like integer
  mark w, like integer
  mark big, like integer
  have the-addition-formula
    mark a, like integer
    mark b, like integer
    call is-equal
      call cc
        call add
          read a
          read b
      call add
        call multiply
          call cc
            read a
          call cc
            read b
        call multiply
          call ss
            read a
          call ss
            read b
  have cosh-near-zero
    mark u, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read u
        code 0
      call is-above
        read u
        code 1
      meet and
        call is-minimum
          call subtract
            call cc
              read u
            code 1
          code 0
        call is-maximum
          call subtract
            call cc
              read u
            code 1
          call multiply
            read u
            read u
  have sinh-near-zero
    mark u, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read u
        code 0
      call is-above
        read u
        code 1
      meet and
        call is-minimum
          call subtract
            call ss
              read u
            read u
          code 0
        call is-maximum
          call subtract
            call ss
              read u
            read u
          call multiply
            call multiply
              read u
              read u
            read u
  have the-step-is-small
    meet and
      call is-minimum
        read w
        code 0
      call is-maximum
        read w
        code 1
  have cosh-is-bounded-here
    meet and
      call is-minimum
        call cc
          read x
        code 0
      call is-maximum
        call cc
          read x
        read big
  have sinh-is-bounded-here
    meet and
      call is-minimum
        call ss
          read x
        code 0
      call is-maximum
        call ss
          read x
        read big
  have the-bound-is-not-negative
    call is-minimum
      read big
      code 0
  show hold
    meet and
      call is-maximum
        call subtract
          call subtract
            call cc
              call add
                read x
                read w
            call cc
              read x
          call multiply
            call ss
              read x
            read w
        call add
          call multiply
            call multiply
              read big
              read w
            read w
          call multiply
            call multiply
              call multiply
                read big
                read w
              read w
            read w
      call is-minimum
        call subtract
          call subtract
            call cc
              call add
                read x
                read w
            call cc
              read x
          call multiply
            call ss
              read x
            read w
        code 0


# GAUSS-BONNET, AREA = DEFECT, for a triangle with a vertex O at the origin. Its far side is the geodesic from A to B,
# cut into n steps of arc w. Along it, theta is the polar angle, psi the angle between the geodesic and the radial
# direction, and ar the area swept from O. Each moves by its increment over a step up to eps w (uniform derivatives,
# as in the theorem above), and the increments obey, at every step,
#   area element   d(ar) = (cosh r - 1) d(theta)   (the disk: integral_0^r sinh = cosh r - 1, per unit of angle);
#   the turning    d(psi) = -cosh r d(theta)        (space/hyperbolic/area: M^2 + N^2 = sinh^2 r).
# Summing, ar(n) - ar(0) = -(psi(n) - psi(0)) - (theta(n) - theta(0)) up to 3 eps n w, which tends to 0. With the
# angle at O equal to theta(n) - theta(0), the angle at A equal to pi - psi(0) and the angle at B equal to psi(n),
# the right side is pi minus the three angles: THE AREA OF THE TRIANGLE IS ITS DEFECT. Every triangle is a sum or
# difference of two with a vertex at a chosen point, and defect is additive (space/hyperbolic/metric), so it holds for
# all. Here c(i) is cosh r at step i, and ia, ip, it are the increments.
rule area-equals-defect
  mark ar
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark ps
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark th
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark c
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark ia
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark ip
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark it
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark n, like integer
  mark w, like integer
  mark eps, like integer
  have the-area-follows-its-increment
    mark i, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read i
        code 0
      meet and
        call is-maximum
          call subtract
            call subtract
              call ar
                call add
                  read i
                  code 1
              call ar
                read i
            call ia
              read i
          call multiply
            read eps
            read w
        call is-maximum
          call subtract
            call ia
              read i
            call subtract
              call ar
                call add
                  read i
                  code 1
              call ar
                read i
          call multiply
            read eps
            read w
  have psi-follows-its-increment
    mark i, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read i
        code 0
      meet and
        call is-maximum
          call subtract
            call subtract
              call ps
                call add
                  read i
                  code 1
              call ps
                read i
            call ip
              read i
          call multiply
            read eps
            read w
        call is-maximum
          call subtract
            call ip
              read i
            call subtract
              call ps
                call add
                  read i
                  code 1
              call ps
                read i
          call multiply
            read eps
            read w
  have theta-follows-its-increment
    mark i, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read i
        code 0
      meet and
        call is-maximum
          call subtract
            call subtract
              call th
                call add
                  read i
                  code 1
              call th
                read i
            call it
              read i
          call multiply
            read eps
            read w
        call is-maximum
          call subtract
            call it
              read i
            call subtract
              call th
                call add
                  read i
                  code 1
              call th
                read i
          call multiply
            read eps
            read w
  have the-area-element
    mark i, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read i
        code 0
      call is-equal
        call ia
          read i
        call subtract
          call multiply
            call c
              read i
            call it
              read i
          call it
            read i
  have the-turning
    mark i, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read i
        code 0
      call is-equal
        call ip
          read i
        call subtract
          code 0
          call multiply
            call c
              read i
            call it
              read i
  have the-width-is-positive
    call is-above
      read w
      code 0
  have the-tolerance-is-not-negative
    call is-minimum
      read eps
      code 0
  have n-is-a-count
    call is-minimum
      read n
      code 0
  show hold
    meet and
      call is-maximum
        call add
          call add
            call subtract
              call ar
                read n
              call ar
                code 0
            call subtract
              call ps
                read n
              call ps
                code 0
          call subtract
            call th
              read n
            call th
              code 0
        call multiply
          call multiply
            call multiply
              code 3
              read eps
            read n
          read w
      call is-maximum
        call subtract
          code 0
          call add
            call add
              call subtract
                call ar
                  read n
                call ar
                  code 0
              call subtract
                call ps
                  read n
                call ps
                  code 0
            call subtract
              call th
                read n
              call th
                code 0
        call multiply
          call multiply
            call multiply
              code 3
              read eps
            read n
          read w
  fold n


# THE SERIES OF COSH, toward proving the bounds the cosh rule assumes. Its terms are t(k) = w^(2k) / (2k)!, so
# (2k + 1)(2k + 2) t(k + 1) = w^2 t(k) with t(0) = 1. On [0, 1] each term is at most half the one before.
rule each-cosh-term-is-at-most-half-the-last
  mark t
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark k, like integer
  mark w, like integer
  have the-term-from-the-last
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        call multiply
          call add
            call multiply
              code 2
              read k
            code 1
          call add
            call multiply
              code 2
              read k
            code 2
        call t
          call add
            read k
            code 1
      call multiply
        call multiply
          read w
          read w
        call t
          read k
  have the-last-term-is-not-negative
    call is-minimum
      call t
        read k
      code 0
  have k-is-a-count
    call is-minimum
      read k
      code 0
  have w-squared-is-at-most-one
    call is-maximum
      call multiply
        read w
        read w
      code 1
  show hold
    call is-maximum
      call multiply
        code 2
        call t
          call add
            read k
            code 1
      call t
        read k


# EVERY PARTIAL SUM of cosh's series on [0, 1] obeys 0 <= P(N) - 1 <= w^2, by induction with the invariant
# P(N) - 1 + t(N) <= w^2 (the next term never more than fills the gap the last one left). This is the bound the cosh
# rule takes as a hypothesis, for every partial sum; for cosh itself it passes to the limit once the partial sums are
# shown to converge.
rule the-partial-sums-of-cosh-are-bounded
  mark t
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark psum
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark n, like integer
  mark w, like integer
  have the-first-term
    call is-equal
      call t
        code 0
      code 1
  have the-second-term
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        code 2
        call t
          code 1
      call multiply
        read w
        read w
  have each-term-is-at-most-half-the-last
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-maximum
        call multiply
          code 2
          call t
            call add
              read k
              code 1
        call t
          read k
  have each-term-is-not-negative
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-minimum
        call t
          read k
        code 0
  have the-first-partial-sum
    call is-equal
      call psum
        code 0
      code 1
  have each-partial-sum-adds-a-term
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-equal
        call psum
          call add
            read k
            code 1
        call add
          call psum
            read k
          call t
            call add
              read k
              code 1
  have n-is-a-count
    call is-minimum
      read n
      code 0
  show hold
    meet and
      call is-maximum
        call add
          call subtract
            call psum
              call add
                read n
                code 1
            code 1
          call t
            call add
              read n
              code 1
        call multiply
          read w
          read w
      call is-minimum
        call subtract
          call psum
            call add
              read n
              code 1
          code 1
        code 0
  fold n


# CONVERGENCE. Halving makes each term at most 1 / N: (N + 1) t(N + 1) <= 1, by induction from t(1) = w^2 / 2.
rule the-terms-are-at-most-one-over-their-index
  mark t
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark n, like integer
  mark w, like integer
  have the-second-term
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        code 2
        call t
          code 1
      call multiply
        read w
        read w
  have w-squared-is-at-most-one
    call is-maximum
      call multiply
        read w
        read w
      code 1
  have each-term-is-at-most-half-the-last
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-maximum
        call multiply
          code 2
          call t
            call add
              read k
              code 1
        call t
          read k
  have each-term-is-not-negative
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-minimum
        call t
          read k
        code 0
  have n-is-a-count
    call is-minimum
      read n
      code 0
  show hold
    call is-maximum
      call multiply
        call add
          read n
          code 1
        call t
          call add
            read n
            code 1
      code 1
  fold n


# A TAIL of the series from term big on is at most twice that term, and the partial sums never fall:
# P(big + m) - P(big) + 2 t(big + m) <= 2 t(big), and P(big + m) >= P(big), by induction on m.
rule a-tail-is-small-and-not-negative
  mark t
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark psum
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark big, like integer
  mark m, like integer
  have each-term-is-at-most-half-the-last
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-maximum
        call multiply
          code 2
          call t
            call add
              read k
              code 1
        call t
          read k
  have each-term-is-not-negative
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-minimum
        call t
          read k
        code 0
  have each-partial-sum-adds-a-term
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-equal
        call psum
          call add
            read k
            code 1
        call add
          call psum
            read k
          call t
            call add
              read k
              code 1
  have big-is-an-index
    call is-minimum
      read big
      code 1
  have m-is-a-count
    call is-minimum
      read m
      code 0
  show hold
    meet and
      call is-maximum
        call add
          call subtract
            call psum
              call add
                read big
                read m
            call psum
              read big
          call multiply
            code 2
            call t
              call add
                read big
                read m
        call multiply
          code 2
          call t
            read big
      call is-minimum
        call subtract
          call psum
            call add
              read big
              read m
          call psum
            read big
        code 0
  fold m


# With the modulus e(k) = 2 / k (k e(k) = 2), twice a term is at most the modulus at its index.
rule twice-a-term-is-at-most-the-modulus
  mark t
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark e
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark k, like integer
  have the-term-is-at-most-one-over-k
    call is-maximum
      call multiply
        read k
        call t
          read k
      code 1
  have the-modulus-is-two-over-k
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        read k
        call e
          read k
      code 2
  have k-is-an-index
    call is-minimum
      read k
      code 1
  show hold
    call is-maximum
      call multiply
        code 2
        call t
          read k
      call e
        read k


# SO COSH(w) IS A REAL: its partial sums are a regular sequence, |P(p + m) - P(p)| <= e(p) + e(p + m), the definition
# of a real in number/completeness (e(k) = 2 / k is a modulus there: positive, and 4 e(4k) = e(k)). Every
# approximation lies in [1, 1 + w^2] (the-partial-sums-of-cosh-are-bounded), so cosh(w) does: THE BOUND THE COSH RULE
# ASSUMES HOLDS OF THE SERIES.
rule the-partial-sums-of-cosh-are-a-real
  mark t
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark psum
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark e
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark p, like integer
  mark m, like integer
  have a-tail-is-small-and-not-negative
    mark b, like integer
    mark j, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read b
        code 1
      call is-below
        read j
        code 0
      meet and
        call is-maximum
          call add
            call subtract
              call psum
                call add
                  read b
                  read j
              call psum
                read b
            call multiply
              code 2
              call t
                call add
                  read b
                  read j
          call multiply
            code 2
            call t
              read b
        call is-minimum
          call subtract
            call psum
              call add
                read b
                read j
            call psum
              read b
          code 0
  have twice-a-term-is-at-most-the-modulus
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 1
      call is-maximum
        call multiply
          code 2
          call t
            read k
        call e
          read k
  have the-modulus-is-positive
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 1
      call is-above
        call e
          read k
        code 0
  have each-term-is-not-negative
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-minimum
        call t
          read k
        code 0
  have p-is-an-index
    call is-minimum
      read p
      code 1
  have m-is-a-count
    call is-minimum
      read m
      code 0
  show hold
    meet and
      call is-maximum
        call subtract
          call psum
            call add
              read p
              read m
          call psum
            read p
        call add
          call e
            read p
          call e
            call add
              read p
              read m
      call is-maximum
        call subtract
          call psum
            read p
          call psum
            call add
              read p
              read m
        call add
          call e
            read p
          call e
            call add
              read p
              read m


# THE SERIES OF SINH: terms s(k) = w^(2k + 1) / (2k + 1)!, so (2k + 2)(2k + 3) s(k + 1) = w^2 s(k), s(0) = w. On
# [0, 1] each term is at most half the one before.
rule each-sinh-term-is-at-most-half-the-last
  mark t
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark k, like integer
  mark w, like integer
  have the-term-from-the-last
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        call multiply
          call add
            call multiply
              code 2
              read k
            code 2
          call add
            call multiply
              code 2
              read k
            code 3
        call t
          call add
            read k
            code 1
      call multiply
        call multiply
          read w
          read w
        call t
          read k
  have the-last-term-is-not-negative
    call is-minimum
      call t
        read k
      code 0
  have k-is-a-count
    call is-minimum
      read k
      code 0
  have w-squared-is-at-most-one
    call is-maximum
      call multiply
        read w
        read w
      code 1
  show hold
    call is-maximum
      call multiply
        code 2
        call t
          call add
            read k
            code 1
      call t
        read k


# EVERY PARTIAL SUM of sinh's series on [0, 1] obeys 0 <= Q(N) - w <= w^3, with the invariant Q(N) - w + s(N) <= w^3
# from 6 s(1) = w^3. With the same convergence lemmas (they use only the halving and the signs), sinh(w) is a real in
# [w, w + w^3]: the other bound the cosh rule assumes.
rule the-partial-sums-of-sinh-are-bounded
  mark t
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark psum
    like task
      take a0, like integer
      like integer
  mark n, like integer
  mark w, like integer
  have the-first-term
    call is-equal
      call t
        code 0
      read w
  have the-second-term
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        code 6
        call t
          code 1
      call multiply
        call multiply
          read w
          read w
        read w
  have w-is-not-negative
    call is-minimum
      read w
      code 0
  have each-term-is-at-most-half-the-last
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-maximum
        call multiply
          code 2
          call t
            call add
              read k
              code 1
        call t
          read k
  have each-term-is-not-negative
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-minimum
        call t
          read k
        code 0
  have the-first-partial-sum
    call is-equal
      call psum
        code 0
      read w
  have each-partial-sum-adds-a-term
    mark k, like integer
    meet or
      call is-below
        read k
        code 0
      call is-equal
        call psum
          call add
            read k
            code 1
        call add
          call psum
            read k
          call t
            call add
              read k
              code 1
  have n-is-a-count
    call is-minimum
      read n
      code 0
  show hold
    meet and
      call is-maximum
        call add
          call subtract
            call psum
              call add
                read n
                code 1
            read w
          call t
            call add
              read n
              code 1
        call multiply
          call multiply
            read w
            read w
          read w
      call is-minimum
        call subtract
          call psum
            call add
              read n
              code 1
          read w
        code 0
  fold n
